<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine November industrial output by sector.</title>
<headline>Argentine November industrial output by sector.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a sector breakdown of growth in Argentine industrial output in November 1996, compared to the same month in 1995:</p>
<p>    Cotton thread:			  57.5</p>
<p>    Cars:				     38.5</p>
<p>    Synthetic fibers:		     32.4</p>
<p>    Textiles:				 27.6</p>
<p>    Tires:				    22.4</p>
<p>    Machinery:				16.8</p>
<p>    Soft drinks:			    15.5</p>
<p>    Assorted construction materials:  15.3</p>
<p>    Vegetable oils:			 14.3</p>
<p>    Primary iron:			   13.3</p>
<p>    Hot laminates:			  13.1</p>
<p>    Basic chemical products:	    12.3</p>
<p>    Liquor:				   11.1</p>
<p>    Raw steel:				10.1</p>
<p>    Flour:				     9.3</p>
<p>    Refined petroleum:		     8.6</p>
<p>    Cement:				    7.5</p>
<p>    Agricultural chemicals:		7.0</p>
<p>    Plastic products:			5.3</p>
<p>    Paper:				     4.5</p>
<p>    Dairy products			   3.3</p>
<p>    Bread and pasta:			 2.8</p>
<p>    Primary aluminum:			2.6</p>
<p>    Industrial gases:			1.7</p>
<p>    Beer:					0.5</p>
<p>    Pharmaceutical products:	    -2.3</p>
<p>    Red meat:				 -4.1</p>
<p>    Plastics and synthetic resins:    -5.0</p>
<p>    Lampblack:				-5.9</p>
<p>    Cigarettes:			     -7.5</p>
<p>    White meat:			     -9.7</p>
<p>    Mate tea:				-29.3</p>
<p>    Total:				     9.4</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
